---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const arrow = '<svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg>';
const schema = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@graph": [
    {
      "@type": "AboutPage",
      "@id": "https://sportsperformancepsychology.com/about/#webpage",
      "url": "https://sportsperformancepsychology.com/about/",
      "name": "About Sports Performance Psychology: Our Mission",
      "description": "Why Sports Performance Psychology exists: clear, evidence-based guidance on mental skills, degrees, and careers in sport.",
      "isPartOf": {
        "@id": "https://sportsperformancepsychology.com/#website"
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "BreadcrumbList",
      "itemListElement": [
        {
          "@type": "ListItem",
          "position": 1,
          "name": "Home",
          "item": "https://sportsperformancepsychology.com/"
        },
        {
          "@type": "ListItem",
          "position": 2,
          "name": "About",
          "item": "https://sportsperformancepsychology.com/about/"
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
};
---
<BaseLayout
  title="About Sports Performance Psychology: Mission & Values"
  description="Why Sports Performance Psychology exists: clear, evidence-based guidance on mental skills, degrees, and careers in sports psychology."
>
  <article>
  <section class="page-hero">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="breadcrumbs"><a href="/">Home</a> / About</p>
      <h1>About Sports Performance Psychology</h1>
      <p>An independent publication covering the mental side of sport: mental skills training, degree programs, and honest career guidance, all written in plain language.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="page-body">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="prose">
        <p class="kicker">Why this site exists</p>
        <h2>An important field with too little clear guidance</h2>
        <p>Search for sports psychology advice online and you will find two extremes: dense academic papers that assume you already hold a graduate degree, and motivational fluff that promises results without explaining how anything works. There is not much in between.</p>
        <p>I want a reader to leave with a more precise question, not simply a new label. A student comparing degrees needs to know which qualification supports the work they want to do. A coach reading about visualization needs to know how to practice it, and what it cannot do.</p>
        <p>That is why this publication connects every explanation with the sources behind it. The <a href="/degrees/">degree guides</a> help you compare study routes; the <a href="/mental-skills/">mental-skills guides</a> explain how athletes train focus, confidence, and routines. Neither makes your decision for you.</p>

        <h2>Find the guide that matches your question</h2>
        <p>You might be choosing a degree, planning a career, learning a mental skill, or browsing the latest articles. Start with the section that matches your question.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="about-strip">
        <div class="quick-grid">
          <a class="quick-item" href="/degrees/">
            <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="#D62828" stroke-width="1.8" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M2 9l10-5 10 5-10 5L2 9z"/><path d="M6 11.5V16c0 1.5 2.7 3 6 3s6-1.5 6-3v-4.5"/><path d="M22 9v5"/></svg>
            <span>Explore degrees</span>
          </a>
          <a class="quick-item" href="/careers/">
            <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="#D62828" stroke-width="1.8" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="3" y="7" width="18" height="13" rx="2"/><path d="M8 7V5a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h4a2 2 0 0 1 2 2v2M3 12h18"/></svg>
            <span>Explore careers</span>
          </a>
          <a class="quick-item" href="/mental-skills/">
            <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="#D62828" stroke-width="1.8" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M9.5 3A5.5 5.5 0 0 0 4 8.5c-1.6.8-2.5 2.4-2 4 .1 2 1.6 3.2 2 5 .3 1.6 1.7 2.8 3.4 2.9.6 1 1.7 1.6 2.9 1.6h1.4c1.2 0 2.3-.6 2.9-1.6 1.7-.1 3.1-1.3 3.4-2.9.4-1.8 1.9-3 2-5 .5-1.6-.4-3.2-2-4A5.5 5.5 0 0 0 14.5 3 5.5 5.5 0 0 0 12 4.2 5.5 5.5 0 0 0 9.5 3z"/><path d="M12 4.5v16"/></svg>
            <span>Learn mental skills</span>
          </a>
          <a class="quick-item" href="/blog/">
            <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="#D62828" stroke-width="1.8" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4 6h13v12H6a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V6z"/><path d="M17 8h2a1 1 0 0 1 1 1v9a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H6"/><path d="M7 10h7M7 13.5h7M7 17h4"/></svg>
            <span>Read the blog</span>
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="about-author">
        <img class="about-author-portrait" src="/images/hassam-shabbir-author.webp" width="320" height="320" alt="Portrait of Hassam Shabbir" loading="lazy" />
        <div class="about-author-info">
          <p class="about-author-role">Psychologist, writer and author</p>
          <h2 class="about-author-name">Hassam Shabbir</h2>
          <p>Hassam Shabbir is the author and evidence reviewer responsible for this publication.</p>
          <a href="/author/hassam-shabbir/">View full author profile →</a>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="prose">
        <p class="kicker">How an article is made</p>
        <h2>The final draft comes after the difficult questions</h2>
        <p>Good editorial work is not one pass through a search engine. It is a sequence of reading, checking, challenging, rewriting, and knowing when another expert needs to enter the process.</p>
        <ol class="process-steps">
          <li><strong>Begin with the reader's real question.</strong> Every article starts by defining what the reader needs to understand, which claims require evidence, and which details could change the answer.</li>
          <li><strong>Build from reliable sources.</strong> Professional organizations, certifying bodies, and published data take priority over summaries and unsupported opinion.</li>
          <li><strong>Check limits and context.</strong> What applies only in the United States, what varies by state or setting, and what the research cannot yet prove.</li>
          <li><strong>Edit for accuracy and understanding.</strong> Names, source dates, and important qualifications get checked alongside readability.</li>
          <li><strong>Correct openly.</strong> Published work is reviewed on a rolling basis, and errors are fixed when I find them or a reader reports one.</li>
        </ol>
        <p>The full process is documented in our <a href="/editorial-standards/">Editorial Standards</a>.</p>

        <p class="kicker">What readers can expect</p>
        <h2>Clear guidance without false certainty</h2>
        <p>Sources are named and dated so readers can check them. Salary and program figures are presented with their source and date, because the numbers change. Where the guidance is general and professional judgment or further training is needed, the article says so rather than pretending certainty.</p>
        <p>An important boundary: this site is educational. It covers mental performance skills for healthy athletes and performers. It is not clinical advice. Our <a href="/disclaimer/">Disclaimer</a> explains this in full.</p>
        <p>If you find an error, an outdated source, or a statement that needs more context, tell me through the <a href="/contact/">contact page</a>. Corrections are part of responsible publishing.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Subscribe band -->
  <section class="subscribe">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="subscribe-grid">
        <div class="subscribe-media">
          <img src="/images/runner-flexibility-warmup.webp" alt="Runner stretching on a track at sunset" width="1408" height="704" loading="lazy" />
        </div>
        <div class="subscribe-copy">
          <h2>Get Sports Psychology Guides and Updates</h2>
          <p>Join our email list for new articles, in-depth guides, and practical resources on sports performance psychology.</p>
          <form class="subscribe-form" action="#" method="post">
            <input type="email" name="email" placeholder="Enter your email address" aria-label="Email address" required />
            <button class="btn btn-red" type="submit">Subscribe <Fragment set:html={arrow} /></button>
          </form>
          <p class="subscribe-note">Thanks for subscribing. You are on the list.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="page-body">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2 class="keep-exploring-title">Keep exploring</h2>
      <div class="about-strip">
        <div class="quick-grid cols-3">
          <a class="quick-item" href="/degrees/">
            <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="#D62828" stroke-width="1.8" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M2 9l10-5 10 5-10 5L2 9z"/><path d="M6 11.5V16c0 1.5 2.7 3 6 3s6-1.5 6-3v-4.5"/><path d="M22 9v5"/></svg>
            <span>Degrees</span>
          </a>
          <a class="quick-item" href="/careers/">
            <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="#D62828" stroke-width="1.8" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="3" y="7" width="18" height="13" rx="2"/><path d="M8 7V5a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h4a2 2 0 0 1 2 2v2M3 12h18"/></svg>
            <span>Careers</span>
          </a>
          <a class="quick-item" href="/mental-skills/">
            <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="#D62828" stroke-width="1.8" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M9.5 3A5.5 5.5 0 0 0 4 8.5c-1.6.8-2.5 2.4-2 4 .1 2 1.6 3.2 2 5 .3 1.6 1.7 2.8 3.4 2.9.6 1 1.7 1.6 2.9 1.6h1.4c1.2 0 2.3-.6 2.9-1.6 1.7-.1 3.1-1.3 3.4-2.9.4-1.8 1.9-3 2-5 .5-1.6-.4-3.2-2-4A5.5 5.5 0 0 0 14.5 3 5.5 5.5 0 0 0 12 4.2 5.5 5.5 0 0 0 9.5 3z"/><path d="M12 4.5v16"/></svg>
            <span>Mental skills</span>
          </a>
          <a class="quick-item" href="/blog/">
            <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="#D62828" stroke-width="1.8" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4 6h13v12H6a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V6z"/><path d="M17 8h2a1 1 0 0 1 1 1v9a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H6"/><path d="M7 10h7M7 13.5h7M7 17h4"/></svg>
            <span>Blog</span>
          </a>
          <a class="quick-item" href="/author/hassam-shabbir/">
            <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="#D62828" stroke-width="1.8" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="8" r="3.5"/><path d="M5 20c.8-3.2 3.6-5 7-5s6.2 1.8 7 5"/></svg>
            <span>Author profile</span>
          </a>
          <a class="quick-item" href="/editorial-standards/">
            <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="#D62828" stroke-width="1.8" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="5" y="5" width="14" height="16" rx="2"/><path d="M9 5a3 3 0 0 1 6 0"/><path d="M9 14l2 2 4-4"/></svg>
            <span>Editorial standards</span>
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(schema)}></script>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .kicker {
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 2px;
    font-size: 13px;
    font-weight: 800;
    color: var(--red);
    margin: 0 0 10px;
  }
  .prose .kicker + h2 { margin-top: 0; }
  .about-strip {
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-radius: 16px;
    overflow: hidden;
    margin: 24px 0 8px;
    background: #fff;
  }
  .about-strip .quick-strip { border-bottom: none; }
  @media (min-width: 1021px) {
    .quick-grid.cols-3 { grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); }
    .quick-grid.cols-3 .quick-item:nth-child(3n+1) { border-left: none; }
    .quick-grid.cols-3 .quick-item:nth-child(n+4) { border-top: 1px solid var(--line); }
  }
  .process-steps { padding-left: 24px; }
  .process-steps li { margin-bottom: 12px; line-height: 1.7; }
  .about-author {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 24px;
    margin: 36px 0;
    padding: 28px;
    border: 1px solid #d8d0d0;
    border-radius: 18px;
    background: #faf8f8;
  }
  .about-author-portrait {
    width: 96px;
    height: 96px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    object-fit: cover;
    flex-shrink: 0;
  }
  .about-author-role {
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 1.5px;
    font-size: 12px;
    font-weight: 800;
    color: var(--red);
    margin: 0 0 6px;
  }
  .about-author-name {
    margin: 0 0 8px;
    font-size: 1.5rem;
    line-height: 1.25;
  }
  .about-author-info p {
    margin: 0 0 10px;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }
  .keep-exploring-title {
    margin: 0 0 4px;
    font-size: 1.6rem;
  }
  @media (max-width: 560px) {
    .about-author {
      flex-direction: column;
      text-align: center;
    }
  }
</style>
